c – Lady Gaga – Bad Romance|date=January 8, 2010|publisher=Musicnotes.com. [[Sony/ATV Music Publishing]]|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131224084249/http://www.musicnotes.com/sheetmusic/mtdFPE.asp?ppn=MN0080511|archive-date=December 24, 2013}}</ref>

Describing Gaga's voice in "Bad Romance", Deflem wrote that it is "at times raw and raspy, not soft and smooth, and incorporates the contrast of gentle and harsh vocal styles, alternating singing softly with screaming loudly".{{sfn|Deflem|2017|p=195}} The song opens as Gaga sings a portion of the chorus, then transitions into the "Rah-rah—ah-ah-ah, Roma-roma-ma, Gaga-ooh-la-la" [[hook (music)|hook]], which she says is an abbreviation of the word "romance".<ref name="abbr">{{cite AV media|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X5Cfi7U4eL4|title=Lady Gaga Carpool Karaoke|date=October 26, 2016|access-date=October 26, 2016|via=YouTube|publisher=[[The Late Late Show with James Corden]]|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161026163523/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X5Cfi7U4eL4|archive-date=October 26, 2016|time=3:02}}</ref> The song then incorporates keyboard sounds.<ref name="leak"/> They are followed by the first [[Verse–chorus form|verse]] and the [[bridge (music)|pre-chorus]] as Gaga voices the lines, "You know that I want you / And you know that I need you". The "full-throated" chorus follows where she sings, "You and me could write a bad romance ... / Caught in a bad romance."<ref name="leak"/>

