In 2011, "Bad Romance" won the [[Grammy Award for Best Female Pop Vocal Performance]].<ref name="marquee.blogs.cnn.com">{{cite news|url=http://marquee.blogs.cnn.com/2011/02/13/53rd-annual-grammy-awards-the-winners-list/|publisher=[[CNN]]|title=53rd annual Grammy awards: The winners list|access-date=January 23, 2011|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110708172128/http://marquee.blogs.cnn.com/2011/02/13/53rd-annual-grammy-awards-the-winners-list/|archive-date=July 8, 2011}}</ref> In 2015, ''Billboard'' called the song "the Biggest Hot 100 Hit to Peak at No. 2", describing it as a "modern classic".<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/the-biggest-hot-100-hits-to-peak-at-nos-25-1/|title=The Biggest Hot 100 Hits to Peak at Nos. 25–1|last=Trust|first=Gary|date=January 27, 2015|access-date=January 29, 2015|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150131015000/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/959606/the-biggest-hot-100-hits-to-peak-at-nos-25-1?page=0%2C4|archive-date=January 31, 2015}}</ref> A 2017 journal published by ''[[Psychology of Aesthetics, Creativity, and the Arts]]'' studying structural patterns in the melodies of earworm songs compiled lists of catchiest tracks from 3,000{{nbsp}}participants, in which "Bad Romance" ranked number one.{{sfn|Jakubowski|Finkel|Stewart|Müllensiefen|2017|pp=122–135}} In 2018 and 2021, ''Rolling Stone'' named "Bad Romance" one of the 100 Greatest Songs of the 21st-century and [[Rolling Stone's 500 Greatest Songs of All Time|500 Greatest Songs of All Time]], respectively.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Hoard |first1=Christian |last2=Weingarten |first2=Christopher R. |last3=Dolan |first3=Jon |last4=Leight |first4=Elias |last5=Spanos |first5=Brittany |last6=Exposito |first6=Suzy |last7=Grow |first7=Kory |last8=Grant |first8=Sarah |last9=Vozick-Levinson |first9=Simon |last10=Greene |first10=Andy |last11=Hermes |first11=Will |title=The 100 Greatest Songs of the Century – So Far |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/the-100-greatest-songs-of-the-century-so-far-666874/bad-romance-lady-gaga-667037/ |access-date=9 January 2023 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |date=28 June 2018 |archive-date=January 9, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230109215229/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/the-100-greatest-songs-of-the-century-so-far-666874/bad-romance-lady-gaga-667037/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|date=September 15, 2021|title=The 500 Greatest Songs of All Time|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/best-songs-of-all-time-1224767/|access-date=September 15, 2021|magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210915162053/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/best-songs-of-all-time-1224767/|archive-date=September 15, 2021}}</ref> ''Billboard'' listed it as one of the 100 Best [[Karaoke]] Songs of All Time in 2022 and 500 Best Pop Songs of All Time in 2023.<ref>{{cite magazine |title=The 100 Greatest Karaoke Songs of All Time: Staff List |url=https://www.billboard.com/lists/best-karaoke-songs-all-time/lady-gaga-bad-romance-2009/ |access-date=October 16, 2022 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |date=October 5, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221016143533/https://www.billboard.com/lists/best-karaoke-songs-all-time/lady-gaga-bad-romance-2009/ |archive-date=October 16, 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Aniftos |first1=Rania |last2=Atkinson |first2=Katie |last3=Bain |first3=Katie |last4=Chan |first4=Anna |last5=Christman |first5=Ed |last6=Dailey |first6=Hannah |last7=Daw |first7=Stephen |last8=Denis |first8=Kyle |last9=DiGiacomo |first9=Frank |last10=Duffy |first10=Thom |last11=Eggertsen |first11=Chris |last12=Fajardo |first12=Ingrid |last13=Flores |first13=Griselda |last14=Glicksman |first14=Josh |last15=Green |first15=Quincy |last16=Grein |first16=Paul |last17=Havens