A writer for the Official Charts Company wrote that the song "indisputably turned Gaga from a pop girl of the moment into an undeniable superstar{{nbsp}}[...] A strange and malformed pop song, 'Bad Romance' was the ultimate vessel for Gaga's unlimited and unbridled ambition."<ref name=LGtop40/> Media outlets ''Rolling Stone'', ''Billboard'', ''The Guardian'', ''The Independent'', ''[[New York (magazine)|Vulture]]'', ''[[Uproxx]]'' and ''[[Glamour (magazine)|Glamour]]'' ranked "Bad Romance" as Gaga's best song.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref name=":0" /><ref name=":1">{{cite magazine |last=Lipshutz |first=Jason |date=March 28, 2019 |title=Lady Gaga's 15 Best Songs: Critic's Picks |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/lady-gaga-best-songs-7881101/ |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |accessdate=March 28, 2022 |archive-date=March 28, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220328152450/https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/lady-gaga-best-songs-7881101/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Cragg |first=Michael |date=April 23, 2020 |title=Lady Gaga's 30 greatest songs – ranked! |url=https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2020/apr/23/lady-gagas-30-greatest-songs-ranked |work=[[The Guardian]] |accessdate=March 28, 2022 |archive-date=March 28, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220328152450/https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2020/apr/23/lady-gagas-30-greatest-songs-ranked |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=White |first=Adam |title=Lady Gaga's 84 songs ranked, from 'Born This Way' to 'Rain on Me' |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/features/lady-gaga-best-songs-ranked-list-chromatica-rain-on-me-bad-romance-lyrics-a9536916.html |access-date=August 25, 2022 |work=[[The Independent]] |date=May 29, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220706154119/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/music/features/lady-gaga-best-songs-ranked-list-chromatica-rain-on-me-bad-romance-lyrics-a9536916.html |archive-date=July 6, 2022 |url-access=registration |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":2">{{cite web |last=He |first=Richard S. |date=August 30, 2020 |title=Every Lady Gaga Song, Ranked |url=https://www.vulture.com/article/best-lady-gaga-songs-ranked.html |website=[[New York (magazine)|Vulture]] |accessdate=March 28, 2022 |archive-date=September 12, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200912130347/https://www.vulture.com/article/best-lady-gaga-songs-ranked.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="uproxx">{{cite news |last1=Gracie |first1=Bianca |title=The Best Lady Gaga Songs, Ranked |url=https://uproxx.com/pop/lady-gaga-best-songs-ranked/ |access-date=April 18, 2022 |work=[[Uproxx]] |date=May 27, 2021 |archive-date=March 8, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220308091749/https://uproxx.com/pop/lady-gaga-best-songs-ranked/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=The 10 Best (and Worst) Lady Gaga Songs of All Time |url=https://www.glamour.com/story/best-and-worst-lady-gaga-songs-of-all-time |access-date=April 18, 2022 |work=[[Glamour (magazine)|Glamour]] |date=December 31, 2019 |archive-date=January 30, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220130183351/https://www.glamour.com/story/best-and-worst-lady-gaga-songs-of-all-time |url-status=live }}</ref>}} For ''Vulture'', it defined the late 2000s and "completed her transformation into a truly fearless, all-encompassing artist".<ref name=":2" /> ''Rolling Stone'' believed the song epitomized the "essence of Gagaism"{{efn|Described as "a relentlessly catchy chorus and a pummeling club beat power a song that's grand and tawdry and joyful and melancholy"<ref name=":0" />}} and ''Billboard'' opined it captured "her grandiose aesthetic, daring songwriting, lyrical flourishes and dramatic vocal flair".<ref name=":1" /> According to ''Uproxx,'' the song had elements that influenced Gaga's later work—"pure pop melodies, nods to her love for '80s and '90s dance, pop culture references{{nbsp}}[...] a radio-friendly chorus that sticks on the charts like honey, and a hefty dose of 'WTF' weirdness that keeps the singer in her own lane".<ref name="uproxx" /> Author Constantine Chatzipapatheodoridis cited "Bad Romance" as one of the signature songs on ''The Fame Monster'', in which Gaga immersed in "her stylized profile of the 'mad artist{{' "}}, who challenged traditional gender norms and sexuality.{{sfn|Chatzipapatheodoridis|2021|loc=207}}

In May 2010, "Bad Romance" became the first video to reach 200{{nbsp}}million views on YouTube, briefly becoming [[List of most-viewed YouTube videos|the most-viewed video there]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wei |first1=Will |title=Lady Gaga's 'Bad Romance' Will Be YouTube's First Video To Hit 200 Million Views |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/lady-gagas-bad-romance-will-be-youtubes-first-video-to-200-million-views-2010-5 |access-date=July 30, 2022 |work=[[Business Insider]] |date=May 7, 2010 |archive-date=June 12, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220612012932/https://www.businessinsider.com/lady-gagas-bad-romance-will-be-youtubes-first-video-to-200-million-views-2010-5 |url-status=live }}</ref> In January 2019, the video reached 1&nbsp;billion views.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Fernando |first1=Romar |title=Lady Gaga's 'Bad Romance' hits 1 billion views on Youtube |url=https://www.easyrock.com.ph/news/lady-gagas-bad-romance-hits-1-billion-views-youtube/ |publisher=[[Easy Rock]] |access-date=July 30, 2022 |date=January 9, 2019 |archive-date=August 2, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220802164743/https://www.easyrock.com.ph/news/lady-gagas-bad-romance-hits-1-billion-views-youtube/ |url-status=live }}</ref> It received 10 nominations at the [[2010 MTV Video Music Awards]], including [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Art Direction|Best Art Direction]], [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Special Effects|Best Special Effects]] and [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Cinematography|Best Cinematography]], winning [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Video of the Year|Video of the Year]], [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Female Video|Best Female Video]], [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Pop Video|Best Pop Video]], [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Dance Video|Best Dance Video]], [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Direction|Best Direction]], [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Editing|Best Editing]] and [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Choreography|Best Choreography]].<ref name="vmanom"/><ref>{{cite magazine |title=MTV Video Music Awards: The Complete Winners List |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/mtv-video-music-awards-the-complete-winners-list-250381/ |access-date=August 1, 2022 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]] |date=September 13, 2010 |archive-date=June 8, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220608043109/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/mtv-video-music-awards-the-complete-winners-list-250381/ |url-status=live }}</ref> It tied with [[Peter Gabriel]]'s "[[Sledgehammer (Peter Gabriel song)|Sledgehammer]]" for the record of most nominations for a single video in the history of the [[MTV Video Music Award]].<ref name="vmanom">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/957071/lady-gaga-earns-record-13-mtv-vma-nominations-eminem-nabs-eight|title=Lady Gaga Earns Record 13 MTV VMA Nominations|date=August 4, 2010|access-date=August 4, 2010|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|last=Herrera|first=Monica|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130523101123/http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/957071/lady-gaga-earns-record-13-mtv-vma-nominations-eminem-nabs-eight|archive-date=May 23, 2013}}</ref> "Bad Romance" received the [[Grammy Award for Best Short Form Music Video]].<ref name="marquee.blogs.cnn.com" /> ''[[Time (magazine)|Time]]'' magazine included "Bad Romance" on its list of best music videos since the 1980s. Its author Claire Suddath said that even if Gaga's subsequent videos were more elaborate, "Bad Romance" was Gaga at her best.<ref name=clawsout>{{cite magazine |url=https://entertainment.time.com/2011/07/28/the-30-all-time-best-music-videos/slide/lady-gaga-bad-romance-2009/ |title=The 30 All-TIME Best Music Videos – Lady Gaga, 'Bad Romance' (2009) | last=Suddath |first=Claire |date=July 26, 2011 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]] |access-date=October 19, 2024 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120129075613/http://entertainment.time.com/2011/07/28/the-30-all-time-best-music-videos/slide/lady-gaga-bad-romance-2009/ |archive-date=January 29, 2012}}</ref>

Writing about the impact of Gaga's 2011 song "[[Born This Way (song)|Born This Way]]" in the 2010s, Stephen Daw of ''Billboard'' called the "Bad Romance" music video a "culture-breaking moment".<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Daw |first1=Stephen |title=Songs That Defined the Decade: Lady Gaga's 'Born This Way' |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/lady-gaga-born-this-way-songs-that-defined-the-decade-8544099/ |access-date=June 14, 2022 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |date=November 21, 2019 |archive-date=May 19, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220519173122/https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/lady-gaga-born-this-way-songs-that-defined-the-decade-8544099/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2011, it was voted the best video of the 2000s by readers of ''Billboard'', narrowly beating [[Britney Spears]]'s "[[Toxic (song)|Toxic]]".<ref>{{cite magazine|title=The 10 Best '00s Music Videos: Poll Results|last=Mapes|first=Jillian|date=July 27, 2011|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|access-date=November 27, 2011|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/468680/the-10-best-00s-music-videos-poll-results|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130214064714/http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/468680/the-10-best-00s-music-videos-poll-results|archive-date=February 14, 2013}}</ref> The magazine ranked it first in its list of 100 greatest music videos of the 21st century and credited it with establishing Gaga's fan base, known as Little Monsters. "It offered a glimpse into an entire cinematic world that thrilled and disturbed in equal measure, expanding the possibilities of what a music video could achieve — and challenging other stars to step their game up at the same time", wrote ''Billboard'' in its listing. "With 'Bad Romance,' she took the old standard for great music videos and set it aflame, then got to work building a new one."<ref>{{cite magazine |title=The 100 Greatest Music Videos of the 21st Century: Critics' Picks |url=https://www.billboard.com/media/lists/100-greatest-music-videos-of-the-21st-century-8466543/ |access-date=June 14, 2022 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |date=July 24, 2018 |archive-date=November 23, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211123225702/https://www.billboard.com/media/lists/100-greatest-music-videos-of-the-21st-century-8466543/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2021, ''[[Rolling Stone Australia]]'' listed it as one of the [[Rolling Stone's 100 Greatest Music Videos of All Time|100 greatest music videos of all time]].<ref name="rsau2"/>

sections.text:
{{see also|List of awards and nominations received by Lady Gaga}}
In 2011, "Bad Romance" won the Grammy Award for Best Female Pop Vocal Performance. In 2015, Billboard called the song "the Biggest Hot 100 Hit to Peak at No. 2", describing it as a "modern classic". A 2017 journal published by Psychology of Aesthetics, Creativity, and the Arts studying structural patterns in the melodies of earworm songs compiled lists of catchiest tracks from 3,000{{nbsp}}participants, in which "Bad Romance" ranked number one.{{sfn|Jakubowski|Finkel|Stewart|Müllensiefen|2017|pp=122–135}} In 2018 and 2021, Rolling Stone named "Bad Romance" one of the 100 Greatest Songs of the 21st-century and 500 Greatest Songs of All Time, respectively. Billboard listed it as one of the 100 Best Karaoke Songs of All Time in 2022 and 500 Best Pop Songs of All Time in 2023.

{{Quote box
| width = 25%
| align = right
| quote = "If there's one song that defines Lady Gaga, it's this one. A highly successful blend of pop and synth maximalism, 'Bad Romance' was a tour de force by all accounts: brilliant lyrics; a shimmery, fashion-forward music video; record-breaking sales; and Lady Gaga's singular voice at its most guttural and raw."
| author = —Britt Julious
| source = Elle (2019)
}}

A writer for the Official Charts Company wrote that the song "indisputably turned Gaga from a pop girl of the moment into an undeniable superstar{{nbsp}}[...] A strange and malformed pop song, 'Bad Romance' was the ultimate vessel for Gaga's unlimited and unbridled ambition." Media outlets Rolling Stone, Billboard, The Guardian, The Independent, Vulture, Uproxx and Glamour ranked "Bad Romance" as Gaga's best song.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:}} For Vulture, it defined the late 2000s and "completed her transformation into a truly fearless, all-encompassing artist". Rolling Stone believed the song epitomized the "essence of Gagaism"{{efn|Described as "a relentlessly catchy chorus and a pummeling club beat power a song that's grand and tawdry and joyful and melancholy"}} and Billboard opined it captured "her grandiose aesthetic, daring songwriting, lyrical flourishes and dramatic vocal flair". According to Uproxx, the song had elements that influenced Gaga's later work—"pure pop melodies, nods to her love for '80s and '90s dance, pop culture references{{nbsp}}[...] a radio-friendly chorus that sticks on the charts like honey, and a hefty dose of 'WTF' weirdness that keeps the singer in her own lane". Author Constantine Chatzipapatheodoridis cited "Bad Romance" as one of the signature songs on The Fame Monster, in which Gaga immersed in "her stylized profile of the 'mad artist{{' "}}, who challenged traditional gender norms and sexuality.{{sfn|Chatzipapatheodoridis|2021|loc=207}}

In May 2010, "Bad Romance" became the first video to reach 200{{nbsp}}million views on YouTube, briefly becoming the most-viewed video there. In January 2019, the video reached 1&nbsp;billion views. It received 10 nominations at the 2010 MTV Video Music Awards, including Best Art Direction, Best Special Effects and Best Cinematography, winning Video of the Year, Best Female Video, Best Pop Video, Best Dance Video, Best Direction, Best Editing and Best Choreography. It tied with Peter Gabriel's "Sledgehammer" for the record of most nominations for a single video in the history of the MTV Video Music Award. "Bad Romance" received the Grammy Award for Best Short Form Music Video. Time magazine included "Bad Romance" on its list of best music videos since the 1980s. Its author Claire Suddath said that even if Gaga's subsequent videos were more elaborate, "Bad Romance" was Gaga at her best.

Writing about the impact of Gaga's 2011 song "Born This Way" in the 2010s, Stephen Daw of Billboard called the "Bad Romance" music video a "culture-breaking moment". In 2011, it was voted the best video of the 2000s by readers of Billboard, narrowly beating Britney Spears's "Toxic". The magazine ranked it first in its list of 100 greatest music videos of the 21st century and credited it with establishing Gaga's fan base, known as Little Monsters. "It offered a glimpse into an entire cinematic world that thrilled and disturbed in equal measure, expanding the possibilities of what a music video could achieve — and challenging other stars to step their game up at the same time", wrote Billboard in its listing. "With 'Bad Romance,' she took the old standard for great music videos and set it aflame, then got to work building a new one." In 2021, Rolling Stone Australia listed it as one of the 100 greatest music videos of all time.

